iple, in a fresh array: by the FFT's\nwrapped product (`FFTOps.fftMulModAt`) when the product is longer than the modulus, and otherwise by\n`mul`, since it would not wrap. Barrett's division takes its products this way (`NatOps.mulMod`).","docLink":"./MPN/Dispatch.html#MPN.Dispatch.mulModW","kind":"def","line":425,"name":"MPN.Dispatch.mulModW","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-mpn/blob/862f63d87fc6e56d648eb33296f1cf7ff688fd89/MPN/Dispatch.lean#L425-L441"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">theorem</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./MPN/Dispatch.html#MPN.Dispatch.le_modSize\"><span class=\"name\">MPN</span>.<span class=\"name\">Dispatch</span>.<span class=\"name\">le_modSize</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">c </span><span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\">n</span> <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#LE.le\">≤</a> <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./MPN/Dispatch.html#MPN.Dispatch.modSize\">modSize</a> <span class=\"fn\">c</span> <span class=\"fn\">n</span></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"","docLink":"./MPN/Dispatch.html#MPN.Dispatch.le_modSize","kind":"theorem","line":416,"name":"MPN.Dispatch.le_modSize","sourceLink":"https://github.com/fgdorais/lean4-mpn/blob/862f63d87fc6e56d648eb33296f1cf7ff688fd89/MPN/Dispatch.lean#L416-L423"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./MPN/Dispatch.html#MPN.Dispatch.modSize\"><span class=\"name\">MPN</span>.<span class=\"name\">Dispatch</span>.<span class=\"name\">modSize</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">c </span><span class=\"fn\">n</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Nat\">Nat</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"